# Commit and push after implementing

After finishing an implementation task (features, fixes, refactors that leave the tree dirty), **always**:

1. Commit with a concise message focused on why
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed)

Do this without waiting to be asked. Prefer shipping to remote so hard-refresh / undertwig.com pick up the change.

Still follow git safety: no force-push to main/master, no amending pushed commits unless explicitly requested, no secrets in commits, no interactive git flags.
